## Installation Steps

### 1. Transfer Bundle to Air-Gapped System

Copy this archive to the target system using USB drive, secure file transfer, or other approved method.

### 2. Extract the Bundle

```bash
tar -xzf {{ k8s_tutum_offline_archive_name }}*.tar.gz
cd {{ k8s_tutum_offline_output_path | basename }}
```

### 3. Load Docker Images

Load all images into the local Docker daemon:

```bash
./scripts/load-images.sh
```

{% if k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry | length > 0 %}
### 4. Push Images to Internal Registry

If using an internal registry ({{ k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry }}):

```bash
# Login to registry first if required
docker login {{ k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry }}

# Push all images
./scripts/push-images.sh
```
{% endif %}

### {{ '5' if k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry | length > 0 else '4' }}. Install Ansible Collection

```bash
./scripts/install-collection.sh
```

### {{ '6' if k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry | length > 0 else '5' }}. Configure Inventory

Copy and edit the sample inventory:

```bash
cp sample-inventory.ini my-inventory.ini
# Edit my-inventory.ini with your configuration
```

### {{ '7' if k8s_tutum_offline_internal_registry | length > 0 else '6' }}. Run Installation

```bash
ansible-playbook {{ k8s_tutum_offline_collection_name | replace('.', '/') }}/playbooks/install-tutum-k8s.yml \
  -i my-inventory.ini
```

Or if using the collection:

```bash
ansible-playbook -i my-inventory.ini \
  ~/.ansible/collections/ansible_collections/{{ k8s_tutum_offline_collection_name | replace('.', '/') }}/playbooks/install-tutum-k8s.yml
```

